<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arusha</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Arusha is a city in northern Tanzania at the foot of Mount Meru, a centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coffee-economy">coffee</a>-growing region and the gateway to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serengeti">Serengeti</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-kilimanjaro">Mount Kilimanjaro</a>. It gave its name to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arusha-declaration">Arusha Declaration</a> of 1967 and the Arusha Accords of 1993 for Rwanda. It is the headquarters of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-african-community">East African Community</a> and was the seat of the International Criminal Tribunal for Rwanda.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/arusha.jpg" alt="Arusha" width="320" height="223" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Halidtz · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arusha_City_view.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
